  - q: "How do I calculate hours worked between two times?"
    a: "Enter your start time and end time in the fields and click Calculate. The tool shows the duration in hours and minutes, total minutes, and decimal hours. The decimal format is particularly useful for payroll because it lets you multiply directly by an hourly rate."
  - q: "Can this calculator handle overnight shifts?"
    a: "Yes. If your end time is earlier than your start time the calculator automatically assumes the shift crosses midnight and adds 24 hours to the calculation. A shift from 10 PM to 6 AM will show as 8 hours of duration."
  - q: "What is the decimal hours format used for?"
    a: "Decimal hours express duration as a single number rather than hours and minutes. For example 1 hour 30 minutes equals 1.5 decimal hours. Employers and freelancers use this format for payroll calculations because you can multiply decimal hours directly by an hourly rate to get a total payment amount."
  - q: "Can I add or subtract time with this tool?"
